# Thread-Safe LRU Cache in Go

Here's a production-quality implementation using a doubly-linked list + hash map, protected by a mutex.

```go
package lru

import (
	"container/list"
	"sync"
)

// entry holds the key alongside the value so we can remove it from the map
// when the list evicts the tail element.
type entry struct {
	key   string
	value any
}

// Cache is a thread-safe LRU cache.
type Cache struct {
	mu       sync.Mutex
	capacity int
	ll       *list.List
	items    map[string]*list.Element
}

// New creates a new LRU cache with the given capacity.
// Capacity must be > 0.
func New(capacity int) *Cache {
	if capacity <= 0 {
		panic("lru: capacity must be > 0")
	}
	return &Cache{
		capacity: capacity,
		ll:       list.New(),
		items:    make(map[string]*list.Element, capacity),
	}
}

